-cgi/image/width=1920,format=auto,quality=85/https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bb44317744228ac5c14eec27c304b11.jpg?s=72&amp;d=https%3A%2F%2Fa.slack-edge.com%2Fdf10d%2Fimg%2Favatars%2Fava_0017-72.png 1920w, https://cdn.tightknit.ai/cdn-cgi/image/width=2048,format=auto,quality=85/https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bb44317744228ac5c14eec27c304b11.jpg?s=72&amp;d=https%3A%2F%2Fa.slack-edge.com%2Fdf10d%2Fimg%2Favatars%2Fava_0017-72.png 2048w, https://cdn.tightknit.ai/cdn-cgi/image/width=3840,format=auto,quality=85/https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bb44317744228ac5c14eec27c304b11.jpg?s=72&amp;d=https%3A%2F%2Fa.slack-edge.com%2Fdf10d%2Fimg%2Favatars%2Fava_0017-72.png 3840w" src="https://cdn.tightknit.ai/cdn-cgi/image/width=3840,format=auto,quality=85/https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bb44317744228ac5c14eec27c304b11.jpg?s=72&amp;d=https%3A%2F%2Fa.slack-edge.com%2Fdf10d%2Fimg%2Favatars%2Fava_0017-72.png"/></span><span class="font-medium text-link hover:text-link-hover hover:underline">Jesse B.</span></a></div><span>·</span><div class="animate-pulse rounded-md bg-skeleton h-4 w-[100px] rounded-card"></div><span>·</span><div><button title="View message in Slack" class="w-full plausible-event-name=tk-slack-permalink-click plausible-event-location=post-in-feed plausible-event-permalink=https://relumecommunity.slack.com/archives/C02MK7D364W/p1793734277920269" data-testid="slack-permalink-button"><div title="View message in Slack" class="flex items-center p-1 hover:opacity-80"><img alt="Slack logo" loading="lazy" width="25" height="25" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-5 h-5" style="color:transparent" srcSet="https://assets.tightknit.ai/slack-logo.svg 1x, https://assets.tightknit.ai/slack-logo.svg 2x" src="https://assets.tightknit.ai/slack-logo.svg"/><span class="hidden">View in Slack</span></div></button></div></div></div><div class="mb-4 mt-4"><h2 class="pr-0 sm:pr-2 md:pr-10"><a class="font-medium text-neutral-header hover:text-neutral-header-hover text-2xl" href="/x/feedback/msg_9B3sDKzGE6yY/can-i-use-urls-that-dont-follow-my-site-structure">Can I use URLs that don’t follow my site structure?</a></h2></div><div class="max-h-[700px] body overflow-y-hidden"><div class="message-body relative w-full" data-testid="slack-blocks-body"><div id="slack_blocks_to_jsx" data-theme="light" class="slack_blocks_to_jsx relative flex gap-2 w-full max-w-[600px] styles_disabled"><div class="flex flex-col w-full"><div class="slack_blocks_to_jsx--blocks"><div class="text-base slack_blocks_to_jsx--block_wrapper break-words font-normal dark:text-dark-text-primary dark:bg-dark-bg-primary"><div id="+kVV2" class="slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text"><p class="block slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text_section_element"><span class="slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text_section_element_text">I like the ability to create a sitemap and structure my site for organizational purposes, but I don’t love being tied to those same structures for urls. Many of our pages are used as small call to actions in person.. like </span><span class="slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text_section_element_text slack_inline_code">/events</span><span class="slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text_section_element_text"> or </span><span class="slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text_section_element_text slack_inline_code">/alpha</span><span class="slack_blocks_to_jsx__rich_text_section_element_text">. I could add redirects, but that doesn’t seem like a good solution either.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[85px] -mt-[85px] bg-gradient-to-t from-background-card"></div><div class="text-link hover:text-link-hover w-full p-1 hover:cursor-pointer text-center">See more</div><div class="mt-4 pt-2 border-t-2 border-card-border flex items-center space-x-2"><a title="0 comments" href="/x/feedback/msg_9B3sDKzGE6yY/can-i-use-urls-that-dont-follow-my-site-structure#comments"><div class="flex items-center rounded-pill hover:bg-background-card-hover p-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" wi